Tue Nov 10 15:30:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- herkos-agent requires hicolor-icon-theme, which owns the icon
  directories of the Permissions window; the OBS filelist check failed
  the build without it.
- herkos-agent: herkosd closing the connection before the first line
  (EPIPE on write) also means "this account is not served" (exit 77).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 15:00:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- New subpackage herkos-selinux (herkos.cil): with SELinux enforcing,
  systemd (init_t) could not connect a tool unit's stdin to herkosd
  (unconfined_service_t), so no tool started (VM test of Build13.2).
  herkos pulls it in when selinux-policy-targeted is installed

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 13:30:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- vilna-home-setup (path and service, as root): a new home that
  useradd made a btrfs subvolume (BTRFS_SUBVOLUME_HOME, ADR 0026) has no
  SELinux label, so useradd could not give it to the person or copy the
  skeleton, and no setting was kept (VM test of Build13.2). The service
  waits for useradd, then copies the skeleton, gives the home to its
  person, sets HOME_MODE and runs restorecon; also on every boot, to
  mend a home made earlier

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 10 09:00:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- Mitos on btrfs snapshots (ADR 0026): herkosd takes a snapper pre/post
  pair of the person's home around an action the tool cannot undo
  itself (Tinta programs saving a file), so it is R2 and undoable;
  undo puts back the changed files through the files tool
  (restore_snapshot) and leaves alone what the person changed since
- herkosd mitos-setup (ExecStartPre, as root): a snapper config
  mitos-<uid> for each person whose home is a btrfs subvolume; pairs
  kept 30 days, or down to a day when the disk is nearly full
- New tool "system" (herkosd system-tool, vilna-mcp-system@.service):
  the saved states of the system and, for an administrator, a return
  to one with transactional-update rollback (R4, after a restart),
  undoable like any other change
- The "Permissions" window offers undo for settings and snapshots too

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Nov  9 18:10:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- New window "Permissions" (herkos-permissions, in herkos-agent): the
  journal of Gloxi's actions in plain language, with undo for changes
  up to 30 days old, and the person's permissions, each with revoke
- herkosd: the person's own connection (not Gloxi's) has
  herkos.permissions, herkos.revoke, herkos.journal and herkos.undo;
  a revoke is journalled

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Nov  9 11:00:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- herkos-agent no longer restarts every 3 s all session where herkosd
  serves nobody (the login screen, GNOME Initial Setup, an account that
  is not a person in system.toml): it exits with status 77, which the
  unit does not restart and counts as success, and it does not start
  for gdm-greeter, gnome-initial-setup and system accounts at all
  (Build11.3 VM test)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov  5 16:30:00 UTC 2026 - Denys <288736242+StDenis1980@users.noreply.github.com>

- New subpackage herkos-manifests: the catalogue of programs Gloxi may
  use (herkos/catalogue, ADR 0017 stage 2 step 7), first the five Tinta
  Office programs, with a vilna-mcp-ext-<name>@ unit for each
- A generic operation ("execute") takes the level of the commands it
  runs, from the manifest's [commands]; an unnamed command is R4
- Programs from Flatpak never get the printing socket; a program that
  takes no folders gets none

